  concept: "Authored objective: Verify reference and calibrate all four channels.\nAuthored
    requirement: Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and
    the level\u2019s verified run history.\nGeneral teaching principle: A feedback
    controller compares measured behavior with a reference and acts subject to plant
    dynamics and limits.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that
    this objective is complete."
  analogy: Steering toward a target works only if the feedback accurately describes
    where you are.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Improved command tracking in one condition does not establish stability
    under disturbances.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Verify reference and calibrate all four channels\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Verify reference and calibrate all four channels\u2019,
    what result or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct?
    Distinguish a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 96, perform the objective \u2018Verify reference and calibrate
    all four channels\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence
    against: Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and the
    level\u2019s verified run history.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion;
    this tutorial does not grade your answer."
